{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For a contract of length k, does it have to start in month 1, or can it start in any month as long as its k consecutive months all fall within the 4-month horizon (e.g., a 2-month contract covering months 3–4)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the start month constraints for contracts, presenting a binary choice within one semantic query."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When you say \"if a 4-month contract is chosen, then no 1-month contract may be chosen,\" is this mutual exclusion global (i.e., across all warehouses, choosing any 4-month contract forbids choosing any 1-month contract anywhere), or does it apply per warehouse (a warehouse that takes a 4-month contract cannot also take a 1-month contract, but other warehouses may)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice between two mutually exclusive scopes (global vs. per-warehouse) for the same constraint, which constitutes one independent clarification question."
}

